&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Engineer — Forward Deployed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UK-based | Edinburgh or London | Approximately 1 day per week&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the future, in the real world.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Principal Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join us in a Forward Deployed role — working directly with teams to turn emerging technology and platform capabilities into real, production-ready outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn’t a role where you sit on the sidelines writing recommendations. You’ll get close to the problem, work alongside the people experiencing it, build the solution, and help them become self-sufficient.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll combine deep engineering expertise with strong consulting skills, curiosity and a practical bias towards delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with teams to understand the outcomes they need to achieve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify where technology can create the most leverage and turn ideas into working solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and demonstrate capabilities, often ahead of wider adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside technical teams, transferring knowledge so they can continue independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed reusable patterns, lessons and platform improvements back into the wider engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted technical partner, challenging assumptions and making pragmatic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help teams make effective use of AI and emerging technology without compromising engineering quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;T-shaped Principal Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;: broad engineering capability across the full stack, with deep expertise in at least one relevant area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering fundamentals and architectural judgement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building production systems across areas such as backend, cloud, data, web or AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong awareness of modern AI capabilities and the ability to turn them into practical outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on approach — you still want to build, review and get into the detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and consulting skills, with the ability to work with both engineers and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic, outcome-focused mindset. You care more about solving the right problem than building the cleverest solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to operate comfortably in ambiguity, learn quickly and build trust with unfamiliar teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in transferring knowledge and raising the capability of those around you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in regulated environments would be valuable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI is part of the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI isn&#39;t a side skill here. We expect our Principal Engineers to be fluent in using AI to accelerate engineering while understanding where it can fail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That means knowing how to give AI the right context, choosing the right tools, reviewing AI-generated work critically, and building the guardrails, evaluations and quality controls needed for production systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll also help the teams you work with become more capable and confident in using AI themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re probably not the person who wants to introduce seven new technologies just because they&#39;re interesting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re the person who walks into a complex environment, works out what actually matters, removes unnecessary complexity and builds something that makes a measurable difference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re comfortable saying &lt;em&gt;“this isn&#39;t really a technical problem”&lt;/em&gt; when it isn&#39;t. You can challenge senior stakeholders without ego, change your mind when the evidence changes, and make decisions without needing everything perfectly defined.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most importantly, you enjoy working with people. You build trust quickly, get close to the problem and leave teams stronger than you found them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The practical bits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; UK-based, with the ability to attend &lt;strong&gt;Edinburgh or London approximately one day per week&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re targeting &lt;strong&gt;January 2027&lt;/strong&gt;, with flexibility to discuss an earlier start where appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re a Principal Engineer who wants to stay close to the technology while working directly on meaningful problems with real teams, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 id=&quot;What-we’ll-offer-you:&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;8044&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we’ll offer you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We trust people to do their best work. That means flexibility over rigid rules, impact over activity, and real investment in your growth both professionally and personally. You’ll be part of a supportive, and friendly culture, surrounded by smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We offer flexible working, including hybrid and remote options. Our office hubs are located in Edinburgh, Leeds, Manchester, London and Bulgaria, with occasional travel to client sites or CreateFuture offices when needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We trust you to manage your time balancing collaboration with client time and focused work. What matters is the impact you have, not how busy you look.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We try to keep our hiring process clear, fair and respectful of your time. We aim to get back to everyone who applies and we will be upfront about where you are in the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It usually looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Call with our Talent Acquisition Team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role specific capability interview&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role, we might also ask you to do a short presentation, a practical or technical task or have a values focused conversation. We will explain what is involved before anything happens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion at CreateFuture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe diverse teams build better workplaces and better products. We want CreateFuture to be a place where people feel able to be themselves and do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any adjustments or support during the application process, just. We will do what we can to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We look forward to your application!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;CreateFuture is fast becoming the UK’s most recognisable digital consultancy, with years of experience building digital products and services for major organisations whilst putting our people first. We have offices in the centre of Edinburgh, Leeds, Manchester and London as well as remote employees located throughout the country.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a team of creators - whether that’s code, project plans, go to market strategies, culture initiatives, marketing campaigns, large language models or people policies. And together, with our clients, we create the future. This has seen us collaborate and partner across a multitude of industries and sectors, with the likes of PayPal, Adidas, NatWest, FanDuel and Money Saving Expert to name just a few.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our reputation as a partner determined to deliver high-quality, robust and thoughtful products has enabled us to scale to over 500 people in the last couple of years, and it is our amazing people - along with the safe, supportive and friendly culture we have built - that makes CreateFuture a great place to work. Don’t just take our word for it though, we have been recognised by Best Workplaces UK multiple years in a row - across a number of categories - and our employee exit rate is astonishingly low. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us on our journey… Let’s create something awesome, together, today.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The bar has moved. Five years ago a strong engineer was measured by what they could build and how well they could mentor others to build it. Today, with Claude Code and agents, we produce quality work at a speed that would have looked superhuman in 2022.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What separates exceptional from good is no longer typing speed or local craftsmanship. It is the complete package: architecture, deep engineering foundations, communication, system thinking, and the judgement to direct both your own intelligence and AI toward outcomes that matter.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exceptional people at this level are not the best implementer in the room; they are the person whose specifications, decisions, and review judgement compound into systems that work in production and that others (and agents) can build on. They are a force multiplier, they hold a room at the highest levels, and clients treat them as the SME by default.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mindset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mindset is the engine, and it is almost impossible to teach retrospectively. You are outcome obsessed, not output obsessed and you care whether the problem was actually solved - you resist the ego instinct to admire a clever solution and ask whether it was needed at all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are intellectually honest about uncertainty, taking a trust-but-verify approach and assuming the surprising bug is the one that will burn. You are deeply pragmatic, which matters at CreateFuture where pace counts: you have outgrown the religious wars about platforms, languages and patterns, you hold opinions loosely, and you decide for the systems in front of you, not the ones you wish you had.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have a bias toward delivery: the smallest thing that works, then iterate, treating documents and meetings as means to that end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And you are relentlessly curious beyond any immediate need, wanting to know how the database actually stores things or why a Claude Opus inference call costs what it does, which keeps you several layers ahead while the rest of the team is still reading the API docs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI as the accelerant&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a Principal to be truly exceptional, this is now already a first-class competency in your arsenal, not a side skill.&amp;nbsp; An engineer who is brilliant by last year&#39;s standards but not fluent with AI is not exceptional in 2026. In practice that means:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setting AI up to succeed.&lt;/strong&gt; You treat context engineering as a craft (the right files, specs, examples and constraints), and you architect systems with clean interfaces, good naming, machine-readable specs and knowledge bases so the codebase is a quality baseline AI can work on later. No separate ivory-tower architect required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reviewing and choosing well.&lt;/strong&gt; You read far more code than you write, and your value is in the quality of review: catching the silent assumption, the security flaw, the architectural drift, knowing where models fail and looking there first. You pick the right tool for the job (Claude Code for a deep refactor, an inline assistant when that is enough, a sub-agent for parallel work, the right model for analysis versus generation) and you know the constraints differ by client, an enterprise like PayPoint or Natwest versus a scale-up type business like Zuto or OAG.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working with non-determinism.&lt;/strong&gt; You see where AI moves the bottleneck and help people left and right of you unblock the value stream. You build with AI components but know success is no longer a binary, reaching for evals, golden datasets, structured outputs and fallback paths as naturally as you reach for unit tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical breadth across the full stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exceptional means depth in at least one area but competence everywhere the system reaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend:&lt;/strong&gt; an instinct for distributed systems (what fails, what is eventually consistent, where queues back up), APIs that age well, thoughtful data modelling, and an understanding that languages are mostly syntax differences you can close with AI.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud:&lt;/strong&gt; cost-aware and security-aware by default, reaching for IaC, composing the primitives rather than stitching together managed services and hoping it works.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data:&lt;/strong&gt; modern pipelines, governance and lineage, increasingly vector stores and embeddings, with data quality treated as seriously as production code because garbage in, garbage out is far worse once AI features depend on it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Web and mobile:&lt;/strong&gt; past the framework arguments, with a clear view on what you would pick today, and able to build &quot;good enough&quot; front ends yourself with AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full-stack here means seeing the platform as one system and knowing which levers matter most. It does not mean front-end work with a few Node.js servers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2571&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System thinking, consulting and commercial judgement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CreateFuture we work in a consultancy context, where many otherwise excellent IC engineers can struggle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You know technology is roughly 30% of the picture; the rest is design, argument and reasoning, commercial and political acumen, and the clarity to frame outcomes for a COO, CTO, CIO or CEO in their own language.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You know when gold-plating is wasteful, you can name when a project&#39;s real problem is not technical and say so even when it is awkward, and you have a strong sense of what is durable versus what is fashion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are not the engineer who introduced the team to seven new technologies last year; you are the one who removed three and quietly made the remaining stack stronger.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership mentality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical work is necessary but no longer sufficient. By default you raise the level of everyone around you, regardless of discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and frequently (documents, decisions, post-mortems, design notes); the written artefact is the machine-readable context we can feed to AI later.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make decisions and own them. You don&#39;t escalate everything or hoard control, and you are willing to be the benevolent dictator when it is your turn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor in AI fluency, not just code: tooling, prompting and review discipline, so your team is twice as productive a year from now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need little line management. You communicate upwards, raise by exception, self-resolve, and can be trusted with financial controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disagree well. You tell people they are wrong with evidence and no ego, and you change your own mind when you are shown to be wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re not looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The gifted engineer who sits in a silo. This is a team game.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The one who is fluent with AI but ships without the guardrails and quality gates enterprise clients expect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The one with strong technical opinions who cannot justify them commercially and gets defensive when challenged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The pure manager who wants to orchestrate teams rather than get involved. This is about setting a new standard, not coordinating it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The engineer who will not immerse in a client environment. This role will mean on-site work and trusted relationships built in person. We are not going back to working away from the client and being bypassed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;About-the-role-and-team:&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2571&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 id=&quot;What-we’ll-offer-you:&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;8044&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we’ll offer you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We trust people to do their best work. That means flexibility over rigid rules, impact over activity, and real investment in your growth both professionally and personally. You’ll be part of a supportive, and friendly culture, surrounded by smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We offer flexible working, including hybrid and remote options. Our office hubs are located in Edinburgh, Leeds, Manchester, London and Bulgaria, with occasional travel to client sites or CreateFuture offices when needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We trust you to manage your time balancing collaboration with client time and focused work. What matters is the impact you have, not how busy you look.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We try to keep our hiring process clear, fair and respectful of your time. We aim to get back to everyone who applies and we will be upfront about where you are in the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It usually looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Call with our Talent Acquisition Team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role specific capability interview&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role, we might also ask you to do a short presentation, a practical or technical task or have a values focused conversation. We will explain what is involved before anything happens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion at CreateFuture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe diverse teams build better workplaces and better products. We want CreateFuture to be a place where people feel able to be themselves and do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any adjustments or support during the application process, just. We will do what we can to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We look forward to your application!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Engineer – Multi-Region &amp;amp; Internationalisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Engineer – Internationalisation Programme (Go, Kubernetes, Kafka, Cassandra, Postgres)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A global sports business is taking its platform international, and we need the architecture lead for the programme. You will be the subject-matter expert the whole programme leans on. That means guiding the shared services work, keeping the flagship consumer app on track, and covering the platform wherever services meet. It is a broad remit, and it is hands-on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The programme&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The client&#39;s shared services team supports several business lines. They are internationalising their flagship app alongside the shared services behind it, such as identity, loyalty and partner integrations. The first target is an isolated region with its own data-residency stack. Multi-region rollouts follow through 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setting the architecture direction across the shared services, and making sure each one can run inside an isolated region with no hidden dependency on the original one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping the flagship app&#39;s internationalisation coherent as the services underneath it change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the seams: how the shared services interact across and within regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data residency: deciding what data is shared, what stays regional and what never leaves a region, across Cassandra and Postgres.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kafka in both worlds: self-contained within an isolated region, and replicated across regions where it is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Terraform and Kubernetes that stand up a new region repeatably, with explicit regional config and visible drift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross functional stakeholder management. You will be the glue between multiple teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first two weeks&lt;/strong&gt; you will review what the client&#39;s team has already built for the first region. You will come back with an honest verdict on what holds up, what will block an isolated launch, and what will make multi-region harder later.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will likely have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stood production systems up in new, isolated regions under data-residency rules, and taken systems multi-region, including the data and failover decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Been the architecture lead across several teams or services, not just one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current, senior Go, and enough React to change it with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of Cassandra, Postgres and Kafka in distributed setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes and Terraform experience at the level of designing platforms, not just using them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The confidence to say &quot;this will not work&quot; to a client, with evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of making the engineers around you better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You do not need&lt;/strong&gt; experience in the client&#39;s industry, or with a specific cloud provider. AI tools are welcome in your workflow; we expect you to understand and own every line you ship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 id=&quot;What-we’ll-offer-you:&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;8044&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we’ll offer you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We trust people to do their best work. That means flexibility over rigid rules, impact over activity, and real investment in your growth both professionally and personally. You’ll be part of a supportive, and friendly culture, surrounded by smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We offer flexible working, including hybrid and remote options. Our office hubs are located in Edinburgh, Leeds, Manchester, London and Bulgaria, with occasional travel to client sites or CreateFuture offices when needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We trust you to manage your time balancing collaboration with client time and focused work. What matters is the impact you have, not how busy you look.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We try to keep our hiring process clear, fair and respectful of your time. We aim to get back to everyone who applies and we will be upfront about where you are in the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It usually looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Call with our Talent Acquisition Team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role specific capability interview&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role, we might also ask you to do a short presentation, a practical or technical task or have a values focused conversation. We will explain what is involved before anything happens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion at CreateFuture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe diverse teams build better workplaces and better products. We want CreateFuture to be a place where people feel able to be themselves and do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any adjustments or support during the application process, just. We will do what we can to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We look forward to your application!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at CreateFuture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://createfuture.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CreateFuture&lt;/a&gt; is an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;AI-native consulting partner&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;where people do work that matters and are supported to do it well. We work alongside organisations such as PayPal, adidas, NatWest, FanDuel and Money Saving Expert, building digital products and services that make a difference&amp;nbsp; while always putting people first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;We’re a team of creators. We write code, shape delivery, build go-to-market strategies, develop AI solutions and create the practices that support our people. We work side by side with our clients, challenging what’s not working and helping them to build the future. Our commitment to craft, quality, and culture has helped us scale to over 600 people in just a few years.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;CreateFuture is a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greatplacetowork.co.uk/certified-company/1572759&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Great Place to Work-Certified™ company &lt;/a&gt;and has won Best Workplaces UK multiple years in a row.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Join us on our journey. Let’s create tomorrow, together, today.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role and team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Principal Data Engineer to join our Data Practice and lead the technical direction of our engineering capability. You&#39;ll work across a portfolio of clients spanning multiple industries, helping some of the most ambitious organisations in the UK solve their hardest data problems.A Principal at CreateFuture operates above the delivery line as well as within it. You&#39;ll define how we solve the hardest data engineering problems across our client base, influence the shape of engagements from pre-sales through to delivery, grow the data talent around you, and be a recognisable voice for CreateFuture in the data engineering community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining and owning the data engineering architecture patterns CreateFuture uses across client engagements — migration frameworks, streaming architectures, data integrity standards, and Lakehouse design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as the most senior technical authority on client engagements — making critical architecture decisions, resolving design disputes, and setting the bar for quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing and signing off technical designs produced by Lead and Senior engineers across active engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying and driving the adoption of new tooling, patterns, and cloud services that improve delivery outcomes across the data practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the technical design and execution of large-scale data migrations — moving high-volume transactional and event data from on-premises or legacy cloud estates to modern cloud platforms, without loss of fidelity or operational continuity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architecting real-time and near-real-time data pipelines for clients with demanding latency and correctness requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and enforcing data integrity frameworks across critical data domains — including reconciliation between source and target systems, anomaly detection, and audit trail requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overseeing the implementation of regulatory and compliance reporting pipelines where relevant to a client&#39;s sector&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with cloud data services (e.g. S3, Glue, Lambda, Athena, Redshift, RDS, Kinesis, MSK, Lake Formation, Step Functions, MWAA, or their equivalents on other platforms) — selecting the right tool for each problem rather than defaulting to a stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practice and people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentoring and growing Lead and Senior Data Engineers — through code review, pairing, architecture sessions, and career conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building CreateFuture&#39;s data engineering playbook: reusable patterns, accelerators, and reference architectures that reduce time-to-value on new engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to hiring — defining what great looks like for data engineering roles and playing an active part in assessment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Representing CreateFuture externally — at industry events, in technical blog posts, and in client-facing settings — as a credible voice on data engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with the Head of Data to enable the growth of the right skills and capabilities to meet client needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Shaping and leading technical responses to opportunities — scoping complex engagements, writing architecture proposals, and presenting to senior client stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Identifying expansion opportunities within existing client relationships — spotting data engineering problems we can help solve and framing them as propositions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Partnering with cloud providers on joint go-to-market activity where relevant, leveraging CreateFuture&#39;s partner status&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What we&#39;re looking for:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consulting background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve spent a significant part of your career in a consultancy, professional services, or client-facing delivery environment — you know how to build trust quickly, work across ambiguous or fast-changing requirements, and deliver under commercial pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable moving between clients and industries, ramping up on new domains quickly rather than relying on years of embedded context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve shaped and sold technical work — writing proposals, scoping engagements, and presenting architecture decisions to client stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand the difference between &quot;good engineering&quot; and &quot;good engineering for this client, this budget, this timeline&quot; — and can navigate that trade-off transparently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud data engineering mastery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can design across the full data engineering stack — from ingestion and streaming through to warehousing, serving, and cost optimisation — on a major cloud platform (AWS strongly preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have deep experience with streaming architectures — Kinesis, Kafka/MSK, Flink, or Spark Streaming — and know when each is the right choice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can model the cost implications of architecture decisions and advise clients on trade-offs between throughput, latency, durability, and spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud certification at professional or specialty level is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of Python, SQL, and Spark — and strong opinions on how they should be used in production data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with dbt, Airflow, or equivalent orchestration — including how to build pipelines that are testable, observable, and operationally sound&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data quality engineering — not just validation rules, but how to build systems that detect and surface integrity issues before they reach consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, AWS CDK) and treating data platform infrastructure as a first-class engineering concern&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ve operated at Principal or equivalent level — making architectural decisions that affect multiple teams, and being accountable for their outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re comfortable in C-suite and VP-level client conversations, translating technical complexity into business risk and opportunity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;You can hold a room on a difficult technical topic and reach a decision — not just present options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ve grown engineering talent around you and take it seriously as a leadership responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 id=&quot;What-we’ll-offer-you:&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;8044&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we’ll offer you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We trust people to do their best work. That means flexibility over rigid rules, impact over activity, and real investment in your growth both professionally and personally. You’ll be part of a supportive, and friendly culture, surrounded by smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We offer flexible working, including hybrid and remote options. Our office hubs are located in Edinburgh, Leeds, Manchester, London and Bulgaria, with occasional travel to client sites or CreateFuture offices when needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We trust you to manage your time balancing collaboration with client time and focused work. What matters is the impact you have, not how busy you look.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We try to keep our hiring process clear, fair and respectful of your time. We aim to get back to everyone who applies and we will be upfront about where you are in the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It usually looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Call with our Talent Acquisition Team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role specific capability interview&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role, we might also ask you to do a short presentation, a practical or technical task or have a values focused conversation. We will explain what is involved before anything happens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion at CreateFuture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe diverse teams build better workplaces and better products. We want CreateFuture to be a place where people feel able to be themselves and do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any adjustments or support during the application process, just. We will do what we can to help.&lt;/p&gt;
