&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Orcrist is building a next generation data intelligence platform using cutting-edge technologies. We&#39;re handling petabyte-scale data with sub-second queries. Our product is a Kubernetes‑based platform delivered as B2B SaaS or as a self‑hosted on‑prem solution, including air‑gapped deployments. We enable customers across defense, law enforcement, and enterprise to turn mission-critical data into actionable intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Machine Learning Engineer to develop and productionize modern computer vision and visual language capabilities across major intelligence and public safety projects. You will work directly with state-of-the-art and open-source computer vision models, visual language models (VLMs), and related AI technologies — training, evaluating, fine-tuning, and optimizing them for real-world use cases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You will work on challenging problems including object recognition and identification, image and document understanding, geospatial data, satellite imagery, and large-scale visual data. The role combines model development with practical engineering: building data pipelines and scrapers, running experiments, and taking promising approaches into reliable systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly hands-on role for someone with exceptional learning ability, strong analytical and engineering skills, and a genuine interest in applying AI to complex problems in the intelligence and public safety domain. You will work closely with other engineers, technical leadership, and cross-functional teams to turn ideas and experiments into impactful capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, train, evaluate, and fine-tune computer vision and visual language models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on object recognition, detection, classification, and identification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build data pipelines, scrapers, and workflows for large-scale visual and geospatial datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiment with state-of-the-art and open-source models and turn promising approaches into reliable systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with satellite imagery, geospatial data, sensors, and other visual intelligence sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of experimental projects and rapidly explore new ideas and technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with other engineers and technical leadership on key initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel every 2–4 weeks for architecture reviews and team events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or higher in Computer Science, Physics, Mathematics, or a related field;&lt;strong&gt; with excellent grade record from a leading university &lt;/strong&gt;(Master&#39;s preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong academic record and excellent analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills and experience developing or fine-tuning AI/ML models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with computer vision, VLMs, image understanding, or related ML applications.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in data, analytics, and data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability and motivation to learn new technologies and domains quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed, hands-on, and comfortable working without close day-to-day management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong team player with clear and honest communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent German language skills.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible to work full-time in Germany and willing to undergo the required security clearance and background checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with georeferencing, satellite imagery, remote sensing, OpenStreetMap, or photogrammetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale data pipelines, cloud infrastructure, or ML deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with sensors such as drones, antennas, or cameras.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background in computer vision research, e.g. Fraunhofer IGD or similar.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Russian or Ukrainian language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interest or experience in military, intelligence, defense, or public safety domains.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first, Germany-wide:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Work from wherever you do your best work, with regular team gatherings in Berlin and other off-site locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility by default: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible working hours help you make work fit your life.&lt;/li&gt;
